# Android-only Tark patches (A1), applied after Tark's shared patches. They
# live outside patches/tarka/ so the Mac and Windows series never see them.
#
# ungoogled's enable-extra-locales.patch (desktop) deletes Chromium's Android
# branch in build/config/locales.gni, which breaks gn on Android
# (components/strings removes "cy", which is then in neither list). Only the
# extended_locales half comes back: the same patch makes Android's
# locale_settings grd emit Welsh paks, so Welsh stays in platform_pak_locales.
locales-android-branch.patch
#
# ungoogled builds chrome/browser/safe_browsing without Safe Browsing: the
# target's base block is `if (false)` and defines no deps, so its is_android
# block's `deps +=` is an undefined identifier on Android. That block (Safe
# Browsing's Android UI and API pieces) is off as well.
safe-browsing-no-android-deps.patch
#
# ungoogled's add-suggestions-url-field.patch gives ResetTemplateURL a
# suggestions_url argument, which it writes over the engine's own; Android's
# callers (desktop never compiles them) pass the engine's existing one, so
# they behave as upstream.
search-engines-android-suggestions-url.patch
#
# ungoogled's disable-untraceable-urls.patch removes Google's RLZ server
# (rlz_lib::kFinancialServer), which Android's RLZ ping handler uses. Tark
# sends no RLZ pings: the JNI entry reports failure without a request.
rlz-ping-handler-no-ping.patch
#
# Android-only code that still names Safe Browsing pieces ungoogled removes
# (safe_browsing_mode=0): download obfuscation's deep-scan check, the
# proceed-anyway pref in interstitial reporting, suspicious-notification UKM,
# the Safe Browsing page's deep-scan log, and an include the removed prefs
# header used to bring in.
safe-browsing-android-leftovers.patch
#
# ungoogled's add-flag-to-configure-extension-downloading.patch includes
# extensions/browser/extension_util.h unconditionally; its one use is inside
# ENABLE_EXTENSIONS_CORE, which Android does not build.
download-extension-util-include.patch
#
# libchrome.so's link: Android's Java UI declares Safe Browsing natives
# (SafeBrowsingBridge and two dialog bridges) and interstitials link the
# settings launchers, none of which ungoogled builds. A Tark file gives them
# stand-ins that read Safe Browsing as off; the remaining callers of removed
# code (suspicious-notification UKM, the tips agent's enhanced-protection
# check, password reuse detection) drop or guard the call.
safe-browsing-android-link.patch
#
# Direct APK ≤ 130 MB (the user's decision, 2026-10-20): libchrome.so is
# stored compressed and extracted at install (Chromium stores it
# uncompressed: 317 MB), and the XR module (Android XR headsets, ARCore) is
# left out.
direct-apk-size.patch
#
# ungoogled never calls ProfileOAuth2TokenService::LoadCredentials, so the
# Android token service's account seeding (the device's Google accounts, from
# Java at startup) hit its CHECK and crashed every start. Tark uses no Google
# accounts: seeding is skipped when credentials were never loaded.
signin-android-no-account-seeding.patch
#
# ungoogled stops registering the sign-in prefs; Android's first run reads
# signin.allowed and PrefService CHECKs on an unregistered pref. It is
# registered again on Android, false: sign-in is not allowed.
signin-android-allowed-pref.patch
#
# Google contacts A1's emulator run found that the Mac build never makes:
# the first-run variations seed (Java, clientservices.googleapis.com, outside
# the net log), FCM tokens and IDs from Play Services (policy invalidations at
# startup; Web Push uses the same path), Widevine provisioning at startup
# (www.googleapis.com), and the new tab page's built-in tiles, which fetch
# icons from freenode.net, github.com and others.
google-callers-off.patch
#
# The launcher label and widget titles are Android resources, which Tark's
# name substitution does not reach: Chromium becomes Tark.
app-name-tark.patch
